& [Question]
  + determine what the user's two-part Cantor runtime plus Cantor SOP seed means operationally which existing Cantor contracts are reusable and what smallest independently governable contract is still missing

& [SourceFinding]
  + the source selects an initiating seed rather than a byte-for-byte archive of every dependency
  + seed part one is an already admitted small Cantor bootstrap runtime capable of parsing verifying planning materializing and receipting
  + seed part two is an exact Cantor SOP installation contract that declares the selected runtime closure
  + external material reservoirs and host prerequisites may be necessary and must be named by the SOP but are not additional initiating authorities
  + every Cantor-managed installed runtime file must trace backward to the seed and forward to one retained verification receipt

& [CurrentRepositoryFacts]
  + source custody commit f41b4d1e6e0f7b838d38993570d17f7ec189f4fd is local tracking and remote equal
  + Cargo.lock is 41561 bytes SHA256 CE078D537A221E448674C60CAC120A3528D06DB83054FCC863EB58C1DEA9BA20 and identifies 157 registry packages zero Git packages and 20 workspace or path packages
  + the tracked tree contains zero root rust-toolchain or rust-toolchain.toml files zero tracked Cargo source-replacement configuration and zero tracked vendor paths
  + the tracked tree contains zero files ending gguf safetensors or bin
  + therefore the current repository preserves substantial Cantor source governance and evidence but is not yet a complete clean-host installation seed or admitted offline material pack
  + D:\CantorBuilds consists of replaceable development outputs and remains outside the selected runtime closure

& [ReusableAuthorityMap]
  + specifications/Cantor_SOP_Seeded_Multi_Backend_Compiler_P0.sop SHA256 819AB41EC28FCE87BEDA7F0CC75A01B3B3D0A5F76BF97581B6CE84FB412415B6 defines a small independently inspectable SOP seed immutable expansion and external successor recognition
  + its Slice5 solution SHA256 F40A7F889694ED7B7D380B1EEAFE820535ECDF0520371283D13BCBEEF2C5712B projects strict source toolchain build runtime and candidate identities but performs no build
  + its Slice6 solution SHA256 35E9166EBABDE4DE98F67676D92C65839D2413E4B7D5AC4C6CD8901824BA0AB3 validates supplied build observations and receipts but provides no production runner or installer
  + specifications/Cantor_Prepared_Runtime.sop SHA256 6FE8F26E983EA7317C6ED08E0300873CEDC2FB3112577ED72050518037F7B302 executes semantic requests over one already supplied immutable environment and does not acquire or install its environment
  + specifications/Cantor_SOP_Boot_Session_Admission_P0.sop SHA256 D5DA781D7DE381B436B0DDDC982226DF84CBE0622555656C737F2FCC9F40E548 proposes one admitted-SOP session while expressly denying process launch workspace mutation provider contact installation and activation
  + these are reusable contracts by exact identity and invariant only; none may be relabeled as completed runtime inflation

& [Delineation]
  + [RIS-P0] pure runtime-closure graph compiler and independent verifier own strict seed profile material node derivation source target layout compatibility verification and expected-receipt forms with zero filesystem process network or installation effect
  + [RIS-P1] materialization executor and observation receipt own separately commissioned filesystem process build acquisition layout permission and rollback effects
  + [RIS-P2] artifact-pack and host-profile contracts own offline versus network source resolution supported operating-system architecture driver toolchain provider and model coordinates
  + [RIS-P3] runtime activation and recovery own service start health admission generation recognition upgrade rollback quarantine and operator-facing status
  + [outside] development-cache retention secret values operating-system installation driver installation firmware remote-machine mutation FPGA and Minecraft remain outside unless separately sourced and signed

& [CandidateDataSurface]
  + BootstrapRuntimeIdentity binds executable bytes profile interface parser verifier materializer receipt capability and admitted host tuple
  + InstallationSOPIdentity binds canonical source signature selected runtime profile closure-root digest and capability ceiling
  + MaterialNode distinguishes seed derived build acquired explicitly supplied generated configuration and external-custody reference roles without collapsing them
  + MaterialEdge binds exact inputs transform or resolver expected output identity target and verifier
  + RuntimeClosure binds every Cantor-managed runtime node reachable from one root and rejects cycles unreachable nodes duplicate targets ambiguous producers and hidden ambient inputs
  + MaterializationPlan orders effectless actions and retains unresolved inputs denials rollback references and zero execution authority
  + InstallationReceipt binds observed node identities layout compatibility verifier results unresolved account and whole-closure disposition

& [ThreatAndFailureAudit]
  + a source-only bootstrap creates a compiler chicken-and-egg dependency unless an admitted executable bootstrap or separately admitted host runner is present
  + a mutable URL tag latest package range ambient PATH cached compiler or unrecorded environment value defeats reinflation identity
  + a hash alone proves byte correspondence but not provenance license compatibility safety semantic suitability or activation authority
  + dependency confusion archive path traversal symlink or reparse escape duplicate target case folding permission drift toolchain nondeterminism and post-verification substitution require explicit refusal surfaces
  + secrets embedded in SOP receipts logs or packs would violate custody separation
  + model weight presence cannot imply provider compatibility model-load authority inference authority or acceptable license
  + an installation receipt cannot recognize its own successor generation or silently activate what it materialized

& [OpenFormationDecisions]
  + choose the first supported clean-host tuple and exact bootstrap runtime distribution identity
  + choose whether P0 admits only predeclared digests or also deterministic source builds and content-addressed acquisition plans
  + define canonical path case link permission executable-bit and platform normalization rules
  + define artifact resolver profiles and whether the first acceptance fixture is fully offline
  + define reproducibility claim levels for source builds that are functionally equal but not byte-identical
  + define licensing metadata retention and operator acceptance boundaries for third-party artifacts and models
  + define maximum nodes edges bytes depth path length transform count and retained evidence size
  + define the exact bridge from existing Slice5 candidate and Slice6 receipt forms without importing their physical effects

& [RecommendedNextContract]
  + select RIS-P0 only as a provider-free installation-manifest and runtime-closure graph compiler plus independent verifier
  + require one synthetic clean-host fixture whose entire runtime closure is small local content-addressed and byte-identically replayable
  + retain all acquisition build write install activation cleanup provider model and external effects as unresolved and denied
  + complete delineation data design semantic refinement dual-hemisphere adversarial review seven-fold explosion justification solution plan matrix phase lock proof and satisfaction signature before Rust

& [Disposition]
  + source is sufficient for architecture input audit but not yet sufficient for a satisfaction signature
  + no implementation download installation activation cache cleanup or physical effect is authorized by this audit
